# Agent team

The project team lives in `.cursor/agents/`. Current members: `coordinator`, `worker-routing`, `visual`, `preview-verifier`.

When a task needs a specialist and none of those files fit:

1. Invent one focused role for that case. Do not create a vague helper.
2. Write `.cursor/agents/<name>.md` with YAML frontmatter (`name`, `description`, optional `model` / `readonly`) and a short system prompt. Name is lowercase letters and hyphens only.
3. Put the trigger in `description` so later chats can find this agent. Prefer phrases like "use proactively" or "always use when…".
4. Launch that new agent for the current task. Do not do the specialist work yourself after creating it.
5. Skip recruitment for a one-line fix the main chat can finish in a few tool calls, or when an existing agent already covers the case.

Do not invent agents that duplicate built-in explore or browser work. Do not create a second visual or worker agent under a new name for the same job.
